WEBVTT

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:31.000
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:38.780
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.890
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.790
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:57.460
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:04.300
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:12.110
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:19.750
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.660
Morning, Nakajima.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.270
Kobayakawa. Morning.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.000
Good morning.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.710
Morning, Yoriko. Morning, Aoi.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.680
Good morning!

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.150
What's with her? Who's
she talking to?

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:54.950
Hi.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.920
FILE. 47
THE TIME LIMIT

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.160
We're off! Good night, Chief!

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.530
Good night.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.400
Night.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:10.330
This heat is
relentless.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.270
Hey you guys! How about
we all go for a frappé?

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:15.940
Sounds good to me.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.040
You mean you're buying?

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:22.270
I'll tell you. The secret to a lasting
friendship is in splitting the bill.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.550
I'll pass!

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.450
How come?!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.420
Sorry to keep you!

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.890
Hi.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.220
Uh...

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.430
Oh...

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.790
What's this?

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.900
How about an expla-
nation, Natsumi?

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.840
Sorry, it's just that I already had plans.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.340
Plans?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.170
Yeah. He's going to teach me free climbing.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.270
Free climbing?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.510
Free climbing. Climbing without using
tools to aid in the ascent.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.420
Oh.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.010
I've always wanted to try it.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.750
So. Hang
on tight.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.120
Okay.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.560
See you.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.830
What was that all about?

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.730
They sure are getting along, lately.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.530
How can they be getting along? They're
supposed to be archenemies.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.770
They're arch-
enemies?

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:22.740
And here I thought they
were just courting.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.000
How can you even
say that?

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:28.510
They're not at
all like that.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:34.020
This is a rivalry like that
of a cat and mouse...

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.890
...an ant and grasshopper...

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:42.490
...or cobra and
mongoose.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.000
I think you've made
your point.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.550
Bring up your right leg! Don't use
just your arms to pull yourself up!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.520
That's it!

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:23.860
You're new at this, so you should take
it easier. Start with the top rope.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.270
I can do it! I'll
try again.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.100
Here goes.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.080
What a
view!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.830
Which one?

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.270
Which one?
That's no good. Don't you have any beer?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:54.330
That's no good. Don't you have any beer?

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.740
That's too dangerous.
That's no good. Don't you have any beer?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:04.810
I just thought it would be nice while we
enjoy the view from up here, that's all.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.780
Hey, that looks
good, too.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.050
Give me a sip. Here!

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.820
Hey, let go!

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.220
Come off it! It won't go down or anything!

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.190
What are you saying? Of course it will!

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.320
Yeah, I guess it will.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.640
Natsumi.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.170
Yeah?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.550
Let's go back down.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:50.390
Huh? Wait!

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.960
What a
freak!

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.490
Hi.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.200
I hear you're Tsujimoto's new toy.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.170
Huh?

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.700
Have you told her?

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.240
No, not yet.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.470
You'd better tell her.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.700
I guess you've been in
my situation before?

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.410
That's none of your
business.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:27.620
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:33.930
The Bokuto Iron Stomach
Battle is about to begin!

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.430
Go for it, Natsumi!

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.440
Use all of your
intestines!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.910
How about
it?

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:47.310
"Bokuto Cafeteria"

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.720
Toukairin isn't himself
today.
"Bokuto Cafeteria"

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:49.850
"Bokuto Cafeteria"

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:53.440
Yeah, he's never lost
so badly before.
"Bokuto Cafeteria"

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:53.450
"Bokuto Cafeteria"

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.880
Hey! I said
wait!

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:02.060
What'd you do
that for?

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.130
I wonder why Toukairin
seems so down?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.560
Maybe he's got stomach
problems or something.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:12.570
What a drag. That's the last
championship of the era.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:16.710
What do you think
about those two?

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:20.540
You mean Natsumi
and Toukairin?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.550
I think they make an
excellent couple.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.280
I see. You don't mind him taking
your partner away from you?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:31.480
Of course not. I'm
happy for her.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:32.960
Recently...

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:37.000
I've seen a side of her I never
even knew existed.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.290
She seems so much happier
than before, somehow.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.660
Hmm. You two have been
together for a long time.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.370
Yes, we have.
It's strange.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:56.110
On the surface, nothing has changed,
but things just seem different.

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.780
They do.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:04.820
"Passing time facing the sunset,
the bubbles drift by."

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.080
Pardon?

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.820
Nothing. Forget it.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:14.970
Springtime... the sound of the
bell of Gion Shojya...

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.960
Uh...

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.350
Hi!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:33.580
Training for our next arm wrestle?
Very impressive.

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:36.120
This time, I don't want you
to just let me win.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.490
I... l'm going to the mountains,
soon.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:44.790
Oh. Where are you going?
Take me with you, okay?!

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.660
Gotcha!

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.610
Hey. Is something up? You've
been acting weird.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:05.110
I'm all ears, if you want
someone to talk to.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.450
Well, actually...

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.150
Well, actually...
Hmm?

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.090
No. It's
okay.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.460
No, it's not. If you've got something
to say, then come out and say it!

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:24.020
How can you call yourself
a mountain man?!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.170
Mountain men
are timid.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:28.440
Huh?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:32.770
They have to be able to think, "If
I go any further, I could die."

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:37.440
If they're not capable of doing so,
they're not capable of climbing.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.450
Wait a minute...

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:40.950
Hey, wait a
minute!

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.820
I told you
to wait!

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.100
"Men's Change Room"

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.770
What are you doing, standing here half-naked?!

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:00.800
This is the changing room!
"Men's Change Room"

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.360
H... How come I'm
so flustered?

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:25.300
Ooh. I think I feel a
fever coming on.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.290
Maybe it's a cold
or something.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.710
Toukairin didn't come
today, huh?

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:49.990
So what? He's not teaching
the rescue class today.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.390
He's probably got other
things to do.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.890
It's lonely, not having
him around.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:11:00.730
What do you mean? It makes no difference
whether he's here or not.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:05.340
He seems to have lots of spare time. Why
does he come here all the time, anyway?

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.540
To see somebody.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.440
To see somebody.
Huh?

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:14.670
A partner you can count on to hold your
climbing ropes is a partner for life.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:18.220
Did you know that,
Tsujimoto?

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:19.940
Huh?

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:23.950
I'll get it.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:26.120
Traffic Section...

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:31.600
Hmm. I understand.
We're on the way.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:36.260
Listen up! I want everyone available
to prepare to move out!

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:41.000
There's been a multi-vehicle accident at
the entrance to the Tokyo Bay Tunnel.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:46.100
Traffic heading to an exposition at the
bayshore is causing congestion.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:49.740
Rescue crews are having difficulty
getting to the scene.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.790
Headquarters recommended
that Bokuto Station...

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:56.450
...give emergency
assistance.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:08.500
Sergeant Tsujimoto, Bokuto Station!
I've got 12 officers with me.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.200
We'll wait for
your orders.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:20.100
Appreciate it. Then you can take
care of the traffic flow...

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.550
Are you from Bokuto Station?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.540
Yes.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:28.420
Are Tsujimoto and Kobayakawa
with you?

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.420
I'm Tsujimoto.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:32.360
I'm Kobayakawa.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.850
Then you two follow me. And hurry!

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.600
Huh? Where are we going?

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.830
What's going on?

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:43.990
I have orders to take you
to the accident site!

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:46.160
Orders from
who?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:53.750
Excuse me?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.480
Did you call for us?

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:00.340
We're short-handed and
need you in there.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.120
The helmets are over there.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:04.060
Lieutenant Toukairin!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.490
So you're the one who
called for us.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:10.490
There's no time for you to change!
You'll have to go in like that!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.220
Be careful, there's gasoline
everywhere.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:14.370
But!

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.030
Wait!

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:24.600
We shouldn't just be standing
here, Natsumi.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.080
Yeah, you're
right.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:37.150
You okay?

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:04.540
I'm not certain.
Yes. Roger!

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.120
What the hell are you cops
doing, anyway?!

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:19.600
Everyone's outside
the tunnel.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:23.290
So you're sure everyone's
out of their cars?

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:30.570
Yes, but I'm worried. We still haven't
stopped the gasoline leaks.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.150
Thanks. You were
a great help.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.350
Wow.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:46.990
So you can say "thank you," after all.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.590
Don't I usually?

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:51.690
You don't usually voice your feelings.

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.860
Somebody help!

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.770
My little boy's still inside!

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:58.630
What?!

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.700
Where is he? What
color's the car?!

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.500
What kind? What's your
plate number?

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:07.640
It's green! It's a Yoko-
hama plate!

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:11.820
I'm going too!

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:12.790
Natsumi!

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:14.720
Stop! It's too risky! You can't go in there!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.620
Let me go!

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:16.850
Stop, you two!

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:21.220
You don't know what you're doing!
There's gasoline in there!

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:25.730
Natsumi. Natsumi!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.230
How'm I supposed to
find the right plate?!

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.650
The gas is leaking
all over the place.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:45.680
Natsumi, it's too danger-
ous! Go back!

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:49.450
What do you mean? You're the
one who asked for my help!

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:51.850
Yeah, I
know.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.690
But you could
die in here!

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:59.190
So you want me to give up? Someone's
life is depending on us.

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.770
If you're scared, then go back!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.440
I don't believe you!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.630
What, you want a fight?!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:10.300
Listen! Your life means
something to me!

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:16.680
What? I'll have you know that
I'm not timid like you.

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.550
There
he is!

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:23.590
Hey! Are you
in there?

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:26.490
Mommy! I'm
scared!

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.750
Don't worry, I'll
get you out!

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.830
It's all right. Everything's
going to be fine.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.910
Listen. I'm going to open up
this door and get you out.

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:43.700
Don't be afraid,
okay?

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.870
Does anything hurt?
Do you feel okay?

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:56.220
Can you turn over?
Can you move?

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.800
Look out!

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.340
No!

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:16.300
Damn!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:20.600
That's not going to help...
you can't do it!

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:25.380
I don't care! If we don't do
something for this boy...

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.210
...we won't be able
to rescue him!

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:32.790
Let's do it,
Toukairin!

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.460
Natsumi.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.670
I heard Natsumi is still inside!

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:55.770
Yes. They went back in to save a little boy.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.050
She's all right, isn't she?

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:03.110
She's all right. She's with Toukairin.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.630
We did it!

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:31.280
Everything's
fine now.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.890
Okay, okay. It's all better now.

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.520
Let's hurry!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:43.960
They're coming back!
They've got the boy!

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:45.960
Natsumi!

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:53.230
Hurry! It's going
to blow!

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:56.070
Firefighters! Hurry!

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.920
Mommy!

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:14.190
Don't worry. It's just a leg
injury, nothing serious.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:18.020
Thank you very much!
You saved my boy!

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.610
What a day!

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:36.340
Hey, how about
that frappé?

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.450
What are you
thinking of?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:43.680
Just because they said we could go. Think
of everyone back at the station.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:45.890
They're all still hard at it.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:46.830
Hey!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:47.620
Look!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.060
Whoopee! Frappé!
Frappé!

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.660
What took you
so long?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.800
I had to thank some people
and other things.

00:19:56.800 --> 00:20:02.870
I was just saying that when you two got
back we should all go for frappés!

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:04.310
Not that again?

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:08.180
Not that again?
Hey, where is Natsumi?

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:20.460
We did a good job, if I do say so myself.
I think we're going to do just fine.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:25.590
You could say we can count on
each other on the ropes.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:29.730
We should go climbing
again!

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:33.400
Huh? What's
wrong?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.750
Natsumi. I've got something
to tell you.

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:46.350
What? What do you
have to tell me?

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:54.380
Actually...

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:14.200
Huh? What did
you just say?

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:19.220
I said, I have
to leave.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.690
How come?

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:38.200
"Tunnel Traffic Light"

00:21:55.890 --> 00:22:02.090
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:11.960
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:18.940
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:19.010 --> 00:22:29.020
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:42.990
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:51.280
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.340 --> 00:22:59.880
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:07.960
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:08.060 --> 00:23:17.530
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:25.010
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:28.440
"Hello and Goodbye"

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:30.910
Let me make this clear.

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:34.920
I thought you were a very annoying
guy from the very beginning.

00:23:35.020 --> 00:23:38.850
I cannot accept anybody who is stronger
and can eat more than I can!

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:41.550
Well, I thought you might not be
all that bad at one point...

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:44.130
...but that has nothing
to do with this.

00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:46.990
Next time on You're Under
Arrest, File 48...

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:47.130
...The End of Summer.

00:23:47.130 --> 00:23:48.870
FILE. 48
THE END
OF SUMMER

00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:51.700
Do YOU understand?!
